Next: migrations

Right now synchronize: true makes TypeORM change your tables automatically on every restart. You saw the danger yourself: the leftover password column, and the need to drop tables to get a clean state. In a real project, that could drop or alter a column holding customer data.

Migrations replace it. A migration is a versioned file of SQL changes that runs once, in order, and is recorded in a table so it never runs twice. That’s the “numbered SQL files” idea you suggested way back when you asked for your SQL in files, and now it becomes the real mechanism.

