Why synchronize: true has to go

With synchronize: true, TypeORM compares your entities to the database on every start and changes the tables to match. You already saw it go wrong: the leftover password column stayed behind, and we had to drop tables to get a clean state. On a real database with customer data, a renamed property could drop a column and everything in it.

A migration is a file of SQL changes that runs once, in order, and is recorded in a migrations table so it never runs twice. Your database then changes only when you decide, and each change is reviewable and committed to git, like your numbered .sql files from the start of this course.